{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"onPictureInPictureChange"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"handler"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@escaping"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Void","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The adapter MUST also invoke the handler once, synchronously or on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"next main-queue turn, with the CURRENT state at install time. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"adapter outlives the SDK session (one player, many sessions), so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"transition that lands between sessions — the previous session’s window","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"closing late, the next one not yet initialized — is otherwise consumed","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by the adapter’s own change-dedup with nobody listening, and the new"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"session starts believing the window is closed while the player is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"presenting in it (measured on the iOS e2e fleet, catalog-pip"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"PIP-ENTER-DURING-* @ 0.50.0-beta.506). The renderer’s dedup makes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"install-time delivery idempotent, so adapters need not special-case"},{"